<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Montagu, 1st Earl of Salisbury</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1301">1301</a>–<a href="/years/1344">1344</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Montagu, 1st Earl of Salisbury, was a close companion of Edward III who helped him overthrow Roger Mortimer in 1330. From 1333 the king granted him the lordship of the Isle of Man, which he secured against Scottish claims, beginning permanent English rule over the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-montagu-1st-earl-of-salisbury.jpg" alt="William Montagu, 1st Earl of Salisbury" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Montagu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
